  "body": "This adds a separately reproducible optimized construction with **211,983,774,909 total variables** (27.62% fewer) and **T < 2^(2^44)**. The dated construction has 292,890,231,905 variables and the bound T < 2^(2^(2^9013)). All dated artifacts remain unchanged.\n\nThe optimized constants now have an explicitly computed catalogue:\n- **W = 185640 = 8*3*5*7*13*17**, with 36,864 unit classes and 811,008 selected primes.\n- **H = 23,150,593**, verified by a complete sieve counting the first 22 primes greater than 324 in every unit class.\n- **F=D=144, G0=480, E0=866, R=H, Q=4^(866H)**.\n- **T = (96*10^13)^13 * 2^8861398783796**.\n\nThe changes reduce the guard's construction work and the degree/coefficient majorants, without a quartic conversion or extra variables.\n\n### Arithmetic and guard simplifications\n\nUse coordinate negation for multiplication by -1, raw addition for doubling, and aliases for multiplication by 0 or 1 and addition of 0. Replace four-square nonnegativity by the typed predicate 8n+3=x²+y²+z².\n\nReplace enumeration of false triples in a cube by an interpolation guard with the same one witness, degree at most 12T+3, O(T²) fixed distance evaluations, and O(T) shared polynomial gates. At a fixed cutoff it has the same existential projection as the old guard on all rational input tuples. Changing T additionally uses the height certificate; guards at different cutoffs are not claimed equivalent in isolation.\n\n### Field and height arguments\n\nThe full-three moduli model's Q-defined normalizer action gives a fibre splitting field of degree at most 144: its Galois permutations centralize a transitive action. Full rational three-torsion already defines every ordered conjugacy Hom group, eliminating the auxiliary Hom-field extension.\n\nQuaternionic multiplication bounds the five-torsion extension by |GL2(F5)|=480. Normality and the local different estimate give common upper-break bound 432 and conductor exponent 866.\n\nThe catalogue modulus is decoupled from P0, which still contains all primes through 324. At omitted modulus primes q>=23, each of the three slope sets excludes at most 14 residues; Cauchy-Davenport makes their sum all of F_q. Explicit checks handle 11 and 19, where the unnecessary -1 restriction can be omitted because these primes cannot divide the odd part of the conjugate-order gcd. The original 44-plane lower sieve, both upper sieves, and the bad-prime set through 324 remain in place.\n\nFor the particular CM elliptic curve, reduction orders over degree-two residue fields factor into small even factors. Every prime divisor is at most the underlying rational prime p. The least formal multiplier divides a constructed multiple, so all prime factors of cstar are at most H, allowing R=H.\n\nFinally use the elementary bound product(p<=R)p < 4^R instead of R^R in the character and conductor estimates. Check the actual uses of the former R>=10^12 floor and remove it. Thus log(T) is proportional to H, instead of H³ log(H) in the preceding optimized version.\n\nM, cstar, ell, and T keep their formulas, evaluated with the changed catalogue and height constants. All fixed scalar and division-polynomial bounds are rechecked.\n\n### Bounds and validation\n\nThe separate degree majorant is **32768*T + 8754752**. Simultaneous bounds remain degree <= (T+1)^2048 and coefficient magnitude <= 2^((T+1)^2048). Convenient absolute bounds are degree < 2^(2^45) and coefficient magnitude < 2^(2^(2^56)).\n\nBoth suites passed locally with Node v24.22.1 and Python 3.12.14:\n```sh\npython scripts/check_construction.py --report build/construction-checks.json\npython scripts/check_optimized_construction.py --output build/optimized --report build/optimized-construction-checks.json\ngit diff --cached --check\n```\n\nChecks include the entire catalogue, exceptional residue sums, 36 exact small-prime reductions, 66 formal-depth fixtures, level-group counts, conductor/cutoff inequalities, guard and compiler fixtures, and 16 corrupted constant prescriptions. Original 25 pinned source files and expression hash are unchanged. New expression SHA-256: `d7a5004eaafa558a36c82c348939d9646b74c7d0cc83fee92b2b0a78c28f15b6`. The catalogue's ascending uint32-LE SHA-256 is `70dc6d12c8ddbed7a5fa1f8f00ce2a6df2b781fe2888a95306e7141ae72b4d4b`.\n\nDetails: [optimized construction](https://github.com/qqwref/diophantine-z-q/blob/simplify-polynomial-construction/construction/optimized/README.md), [prime catalogue proof](https://github.com/qqwref/diophantine-z-q/blob/simplify-polynomial-construction/construction/optimized/prime-catalogue.md), [field and cutoff proof](https://github.com/qqwref/diophantine-z-q/blob/simplify-polynomial-construction/construction/optimized/cutoff.md).\n\nThese are proposed arguments within the manuscript's stated arithmetic and geometric framework. Finite checks do not machine-formalize the geometric or prime-pattern proofs or independently certify the main theorem. Implementation and arguments were developed with ChatGPT/Codex at the repository owner's request; no independent human review or completed Lean verification is claimed.",
